A python based computer game

Run Platstart.py with Python and pygame installed.
Move with arrow keys or A/D, and jump with Space, Up, or W.

There are 11 levels: the expanded original and 10 additional worlds.
Worlds are 2400-4000 pixels wide and 1200-1600 pixels tall. The camera follows
you horizontally and vertically. Collect every coin in a level, then reach
the exit at the far right to advance. Finish level 11 to win; R plays again.
Touching the enemy or falling off-screen loses ALL coins and restarts level 1.

Enemy AI is in enemyai.py. It uses A* over standing positions on platforms.
Walk, jump, and drop edges are simulated using the same physics.py movement
and collision code as the player. The enemy executes the planned jump inputs,
lands on platforms, and replans between moves when your destination changes.
For airborne players, it predicts a landing platform. If there is no physically
reachable route, it waits instead of flying or teleporting.

Level layouts, coin placements, and exits are in levels.py.

Run the focused tests with: python -B -m unittest -v test_game
Tests verify every navigation edge, player routes to every coin and exit,
enemy pursuit up and down each world, A* shortest paths, progression, and death.